# Single-page app: every path is handled by the React router, so anything that
# is not a real file has to be served index.html rather than a 404.
#
# This is not cosmetic here. The links people actually receive are all deep
# links into the app: /ticket?t=... in confirmation emails, /rsvp/<id> shared
# with students, /reset-password?token=... in recovery emails. Without this
# rule every one of them 404s on a fresh visit, because no /ticket/index.html
# exists on disk.
#
# Used by Netlify and Cloudflare Pages. Vercel reads vercel.json instead.
/*  /index.html  200
